OpenRC Scripts for Miniflux on Alpine Linux
============================================

Files:
  miniflux                  OpenRC init script
  miniflux.conf             OpenRC conf.d (supervisor settings)
  miniflux.conf.application Miniflux application config (SQLite defaults)
  miniflux.pre-install      User/group creation script
  logrotate-miniflux        Logrotate configuration
  install.sh                Convenience install script (run as root, builds from source, creates admin)

Quick install (as root):
  sh packaging/openrc/install.sh

This will:
  - Build the miniflux binary from source (SQLite support included)
  - Create the miniflux system user/group
  - Prompt for admin username and password (or skip to create no admin)
  - Create /var/lib/miniflux/ for the SQLite database
  - Install the init script, OpenRC config, and application config
  - Install logrotate configuration
  - Initialize the database file
  - Start the service and create the admin user via the miniflux CLI

The config file (/etc/miniflux.conf) is installed clean (mode 0644) — no admin
credentials are ever written to it.  Admin creation is done via the miniflux
CLI after the service starts:

  - Interactive mode (default):  miniflux --config-file /etc/miniflux.conf --create-admin
                                  (requires a TTY)
  - Non-interactive mode:        --admin-user/--admin-pass flags to install.sh.
                                  Password is passed via ADMIN_PASSWORD_FILE (a
                                  0600 root-only temp file), never in argv.

Security notes:
  - /etc/miniflux.conf holds no secrets (0644 is safe).
  - In non-interactive mode, the password lives briefly in a 0600 root-owned
    temp file, deleted after admin creation. It is NOT passed on the miniflux
    command line (would be visible in `ps`).
  - --admin-pass on the install.sh command line is visible in shell history.
    Prefer interactive mode on shared hosts.
  - logrotate uses copytruncate (no service restart, no downtime).
  - The miniflux daemon runs as the unprivileged `miniflux` user.

Install from pre-built binary (e.g., from apk):
  sh packaging/openrc/install.sh --no-build

Custom options:
  sh packaging/openrc/install.sh --sqlite-dir /path/to/db
  sh packaging/openrc/install.sh --no-enable    # don't enable/start at boot
  sh packaging/openrc/install.sh --no-backup    # don't backup existing config
  sh packaging/openrc/install.sh --no-build     # skip building from source
  sh packaging/openrc/install.sh --no-admin     # skip admin creation entirely
  sh packaging/openrc/install.sh --admin-user myuser --admin-pass mypass  # non-interactive admin

Manual install (without install.sh):
  1. cp packaging/openrc/miniflux /etc/init.d/miniflux
  2. cp packaging/openrc/miniflux.conf /etc/conf.d/miniflux
  3. cp packaging/openrc/miniflux.conf.application /etc/miniflux.conf
  4. cp packaging/openrc/logrotate-miniflux /etc/logrotate.d/miniflux
  5. rc-update add miniflux default
  6. service miniflux start

  To create an admin user interactively:
  7. service miniflux start
  8. miniflux --config-file /etc/miniflux.conf --create-admin

Configuration:
  Edit /etc/miniflux.conf to customize settings. Key defaults:
    - DATABASE_TYPE=sqlite
    - DATABASE_URL=/var/lib/miniflux/miniflux.db
    - LISTEN_ADDR=127.0.0.1:8080
    - RUN_MIGRATIONS=1
